1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,878
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor… ♪

2
00:00:04,421 --> 00:00:07,465
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

3
00:00:09,259 --> 00:00:10,719
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

4
00:00:10,802 --> 00:00:12,971
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

5
00:00:13,054 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ One cut and it's over. ♪

6
00:00:17,308 --> 00:00:20,520
OSCAR: Looks like my prayers to
Saint Anthony actually worked.

7
00:00:20,603 --> 00:00:22,564
You still managed to find me, buddy.

8
00:00:22,647 --> 00:00:23,648
Didn't you?

9
00:00:23,732 --> 00:00:26,401
Isn't he Tatoy's best friend?

10
00:00:26,484 --> 00:00:28,278
The one we saw in the photo album?

11
00:00:28,361 --> 00:00:30,238
ATOY: As a matter of fact,

12
00:00:30,321 --> 00:00:31,448
he's here right now.

13
00:00:31,531 --> 00:00:33,074
- Oscar.
- Good evening, everyone!

14
00:00:33,158 --> 00:00:34,868
Can Oka stay here for a while?

15
00:00:34,951 --> 00:00:36,995
Oka, okak, okak.
[chuckles]

16
00:00:37,078 --> 00:00:38,580
He's my friend.

17
00:00:38,663 --> 00:00:40,165
ATOY: I can't just abandon him.

18
00:00:40,248 --> 00:00:43,752
AUDREY: Do you really think he's still
the same Oscar you used to know?

19
00:00:43,835 --> 00:00:48,006
What if you're bringing a
dangerous person into our home?

20
00:00:48,089 --> 00:00:50,008
OSCAR: Got you, Ibyang! Aargh!
[gasps]

21
00:00:50,091 --> 00:00:50,633
Ibyang, sorry.

22
00:00:50,717 --> 00:00:52,010
What are you doing to my child?!

23
00:00:52,093 --> 00:00:53,470
- Ibyang, come here!
- Nothing--

24
00:00:53,553 --> 00:00:55,722
- I wasn't doing any--
- Don't hurt Ibyang!

25
00:00:55,805 --> 00:00:56,806
He's my friend.

26
00:00:56,890 --> 00:00:57,932
Oh, is he Okra?

27
00:00:58,016 --> 00:01:00,810
AME: We have a group that
handles different missions.

28
00:01:00,894 --> 00:01:01,519
Can I join?

29
00:01:01,603 --> 00:01:03,188
What are the requirements?

30
00:01:03,271 --> 00:01:05,190
You need a code name!

31
00:01:05,273 --> 00:01:06,274
Oskarayom.

32
00:01:06,357 --> 00:01:07,734
I don't trust him,

33
00:01:07,817 --> 00:01:09,736
and I don't want him around our daughters.

34
00:01:09,819 --> 00:01:11,488
AUDREY: It's a mother's instinct.

35
00:01:11,571 --> 00:01:12,822
You have to trust me!

36
00:01:12,906 --> 00:01:15,366
I don't want the two of you fighting
because of me.

37
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:16,659
You can stay at the shop instead.

38
00:01:16,743 --> 00:01:18,411
Are you sure Audrey won't get mad at you?

39
00:01:18,495 --> 00:01:19,621
ARTEM: Oscar is alive.

40
00:01:19,704 --> 00:01:21,039
Aren't you worried?

41
00:01:21,122 --> 00:01:23,583
If he can survive the explosion,

42
00:01:23,666 --> 00:01:25,210
what about Atoy?

43
00:01:25,293 --> 00:01:30,465
Until I see Atoy's dead body
on the ground,

44
00:01:30,548 --> 00:01:33,134
I will consider him alive.

45
00:01:33,218 --> 00:01:35,303
♪ Like a bubble, like a bubble ♪

46
00:01:35,386 --> 00:01:38,139
♪ When it bursts,
it knows how to hit its mark ♪

47
00:01:39,808 --> 00:01:41,476
ATOY: Buddy, come on in.

48
00:01:42,602 --> 00:01:43,311
Godmother.

49
00:01:43,394 --> 00:01:44,646
Oh? Oh.

50
00:01:44,729 --> 00:01:46,815
Godmother, this is Oka.

51
00:01:46,898 --> 00:01:48,691
He's the one I've been telling you about.

52
00:01:48,775 --> 00:01:49,776
Oka, this is Godmother Cita.

53
00:01:49,859 --> 00:01:51,361
She's Karla's mother.

54
00:01:51,444 --> 00:01:54,114
Oscar, Oka, is my buddy.

55
00:01:54,906 --> 00:01:57,951
He's going to use the vacant room
upstairs for now, Godmother.

56
00:01:58,034 --> 00:01:59,953
Ahh. Yes, yes.
[chuckles softly]

57
00:02:00,036 --> 00:02:00,745
OSCAR: Good evening, Ma'am.

58
00:02:00,829 --> 00:02:02,497
Mother? Are you sure she's the mother?

59
00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:03,456
Mm-hmm.

60
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:05,250
She's more like Karla's older sister.

61
00:02:05,333 --> 00:02:07,210
- Oh my.
- Yes.

62
00:02:07,293 --> 00:02:08,545
Oh, Lord, forgive me.

63
00:02:08,628 --> 00:02:10,797
You're just buttering me up. I’m old.

64
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:11,840
Me? Buttering you up?

65
00:02:11,923 --> 00:02:13,216
Where? Where’s the old woman?

66
00:02:13,299 --> 00:02:14,717
[chuckles]
I don't see any old woman around here.

67
00:02:14,801 --> 00:02:15,301
[chuckles]

68
00:02:15,385 --> 00:02:15,927
You're still very young, Ma'am.

69
00:02:16,010 --> 00:02:17,720
- Oh, no. No, no.
- Don't try to sweet-talk me.

70
00:02:17,804 --> 00:02:20,140
Wait. Let me talk to Jesabel

71
00:02:20,223 --> 00:02:22,016
and have the room upstairs fixed up.

72
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:22,725
- ATOY: Sure, Godmother.
- I'll be back.

73
00:02:22,809 --> 00:02:23,810
Okay.

74
00:02:24,352 --> 00:02:26,271
There you go, buddy, welcome.

75
00:02:27,230 --> 00:02:28,398
This is nice, Toy.

76
00:02:29,149 --> 00:02:30,316
What's this? A tailoring shop?

77
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:30,942
Mm-hmm.

78
00:02:31,025 --> 00:02:32,569
I inherited it from my father.

79
00:02:33,736 --> 00:02:35,196
So, I'm carrying on the business.

80
00:02:36,364 --> 00:02:38,491
You're really lucky, buddy.

81
00:02:38,575 --> 00:02:39,617
[chuckles softly]

82
00:02:39,701 --> 00:02:43,454
You have a family; you have a business.

83
00:02:43,538 --> 00:02:44,956
[pensive music playing]

84
00:02:45,039 --> 00:02:46,040
You're doing great.

85
00:02:47,834 --> 00:02:50,378
Buddy, don't worry.

86
00:02:51,713 --> 00:02:54,424
One day, you'll find
everything you're looking for.

87
00:02:55,008 --> 00:02:56,676
You'll have a family.

88
00:02:56,759 --> 00:02:58,136
You'll have a business.

89
00:02:59,178 --> 00:03:00,930
All of that will be yours, and more.

90
00:03:01,598 --> 00:03:03,474
[suspicious music playing]

91
00:03:03,558 --> 00:03:04,559
[clicks tongue]

92
00:03:04,642 --> 00:03:05,810
I'm happy for you, buddy.

93
00:03:05,894 --> 00:03:07,270
- Thanks, buddy.
- [chuckles softly]

94
00:03:08,730 --> 00:03:10,106
Here.

95
00:03:10,189 --> 00:03:12,901
[theme music playing]

96
00:03:13,902 --> 00:03:16,279
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor… ♪

97
00:03:16,362 --> 00:03:18,239
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

98
00:03:21,784 --> 00:03:23,745
♪ Wait a moment, Mr. Tailor ♪

99
00:03:23,828 --> 00:03:25,830
♪ Can you be the one to sew ♪

100
00:03:25,914 --> 00:03:29,208
♪ The hole in my polo
that's right under the armpit ♪

101
00:03:29,292 --> 00:03:31,461
♪ In every cut of cloth ♪

102
00:03:31,544 --> 00:03:33,212
♪ There’s a secret behind it ♪

103
00:03:33,296 --> 00:03:35,215
♪ If your measurements are wrong,

104
00:03:35,298 --> 00:03:39,385
the whole fit turns crooked… ♪

105
00:03:40,345 --> 00:03:40,970
[gunshots]

106
00:03:41,054 --> 00:03:42,722
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

107
00:03:42,805 --> 00:03:44,724
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

108
00:03:44,807 --> 00:03:46,184
[music swells]

109
00:03:48,603 --> 00:03:50,355
[music fades]

110
00:03:52,982 --> 00:03:54,275
Hey, Karla.

111
00:03:54,901 --> 00:04:00,531
What's this we're hearing about
Brother Atoy and Audrey fighting?

112
00:04:00,615 --> 00:04:02,200
SIONY: Is it because of Oscar,

113
00:04:02,283 --> 00:04:03,701
Atoy's friend?

114
00:04:03,785 --> 00:04:05,578
The new guy?

115
00:04:05,662 --> 00:04:07,247
Oh, Siony!

116
00:04:07,330 --> 00:04:09,582
Don't act like you don't know anything.

117
00:04:09,666 --> 00:04:11,501
Your gossip radar is always on!

118
00:04:11,584 --> 00:04:13,127
NESTOR: Why are you even asking?

119
00:04:13,211 --> 00:04:14,212
Just confirming!

120
00:04:14,295 --> 00:04:14,921
NESTOR: Hmm!

121
00:04:15,004 --> 00:04:16,047
KARLA: Just confirming, huh?

122
00:04:16,130 --> 00:04:17,715
VELMA: Wait a second.

123
00:04:17,799 --> 00:04:20,051
What's this Oscar guy look like?

124
00:04:20,134 --> 00:04:21,261
Is he handsome?

125
00:04:21,344 --> 00:04:22,303
Oh.

126
00:04:22,387 --> 00:04:24,180
- Goodness.
- AME: Yes.

127
00:04:24,264 --> 00:04:25,890
Charming.

128
00:04:25,974 --> 00:04:27,684
But Atoy is still more handsome,
of course.

129
00:04:27,767 --> 00:04:28,476
EMERSON: Mmm-mmm.

130
00:04:28,559 --> 00:04:31,437
- KARLA: Whoa. Move on already, sis.
- We didn't even get to see him!

131
00:04:31,521 --> 00:04:33,731
You know what?
Why don't we visit Brother Atoy?

132
00:04:33,815 --> 00:04:35,149
Then pretend we've run out of salt!

133
00:04:35,233 --> 00:04:35,817
Oh, right.

134
00:04:35,900 --> 00:04:36,859
[overlapping chatter]

135
00:04:36,943 --> 00:04:37,986
Hey, not now, sis.

136
00:04:38,069 --> 00:04:39,862
The couple is fighting, right?

137
00:04:39,946 --> 00:04:41,781
They're saltier than salt itself.

138
00:04:41,864 --> 00:04:42,448
PALDO: Oh?

139
00:04:43,324 --> 00:04:45,827
But Karla, admit it.

140
00:04:47,370 --> 00:04:49,831
Why did they… have a lovers' quarrel?

141
00:04:51,916 --> 00:04:54,460
Well, to cut the long story short…

142
00:04:56,629 --> 00:04:59,549
Audrey thought Oscar was a bad person.

143
00:05:00,174 --> 00:05:02,593
That's exactly what we thought
at first too.

144
00:05:02,677 --> 00:05:03,678
SIONY: Ahh…

145
00:05:03,761 --> 00:05:05,388
Hmm, that…

146
00:05:06,681 --> 00:05:09,434
sounds like mistaken identity.

147
00:05:10,268 --> 00:05:12,312
But do you remember?

148
00:05:12,395 --> 00:05:18,526
You all thought Uno had
bad intentions, but…

149
00:05:18,609 --> 00:05:20,069
as it turned out,

150
00:05:20,153 --> 00:05:21,863
he was actually on our side.

151
00:05:21,946 --> 00:05:23,698
NESTOR: That's true.

152
00:05:24,282 --> 00:05:27,035
Brother Oka actually seems all right.

153
00:05:27,118 --> 00:05:29,996
He still exuded good vibes,
even after I hit him with a cooking pot.

154
00:05:30,079 --> 00:05:33,249
Brother Emerson, let's go visit Uno.

155
00:05:33,875 --> 00:05:34,959
Sure.

156
00:05:35,043 --> 00:05:35,918
[sneaky music playing]

157
00:05:36,002 --> 00:05:37,420
Let's visit Uno.

158
00:05:37,503 --> 00:05:38,629
Brother Kurt, can I have some soup?

159
00:05:38,713 --> 00:05:39,547
But…

160
00:05:40,882 --> 00:05:42,759
listen up because I have something
to tell you.

161
00:05:42,842 --> 00:05:44,343
[music continues]

162
00:05:44,427 --> 00:05:49,098
Uno and that Oscar
guy are completely different.

163
00:05:49,182 --> 00:05:50,558
- Hmm. No, just no.
- How can you say that?

164
00:05:50,641 --> 00:05:52,351
I just know, Ame.

165
00:05:53,227 --> 00:05:55,146
I just have this… feeling.

166
00:05:55,229 --> 00:05:57,106
I can't explain it.

167
00:05:57,190 --> 00:05:59,525
There's something about him,
a vibe that just…

168
00:05:59,609 --> 00:06:01,402
doesn't feel right.

169
00:06:01,486 --> 00:06:02,695
NESTOR: Oh, Emerson, oh!

170
00:06:03,488 --> 00:06:05,823
You're just jealous of Atoy's OG friend

171
00:06:05,907 --> 00:06:07,575
because he's just as handsome as Atoy.

172
00:06:07,658 --> 00:06:11,079
- Oh.
- [teasing & laughing] No! Not at all!

173
00:06:11,662 --> 00:06:12,955
I'm more handsome than him.

174
00:06:13,039 --> 00:06:13,956
Just ask Denden.

175
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,958
[teasing]
KARLA: Whatever you say.

176
00:06:16,042 --> 00:06:17,752
Denden's annoyed with you these days,

177
00:06:17,835 --> 00:06:19,629
so nobody here thinks
you're handsome anymore.

178
00:06:19,712 --> 00:06:20,630
KARLA: Whoa.

179
00:06:20,713 --> 00:06:22,548
- JONA: Denden was the only one--
- Except maybe Father Peping,

180
00:06:22,632 --> 00:06:23,633
when he's not wearing his glasses.

181
00:06:23,716 --> 00:06:25,635
[teasing & laughing]
KARLA: Oh my! Hey!

182
00:06:25,718 --> 00:06:27,345
[playful music playing]

183
00:06:27,428 --> 00:06:30,848
PALDO: Hmm. This is delicious. Eat up!

184
00:06:30,932 --> 00:06:32,850
ATOY: Here, this belonged to
my father, buddy.

185
00:06:32,934 --> 00:06:34,936
He was the original Master Cutter here.

186
00:06:35,019 --> 00:06:36,270
Oh, he was really famous around here.

187
00:06:36,354 --> 00:06:38,773
Everyone wanted him to make their clothes.

188
00:06:38,856 --> 00:06:41,734
- Master Cutter. Nice!
- Yeah.

189
00:06:42,443 --> 00:06:44,070
[chuckles softly]

190
00:06:44,695 --> 00:06:45,446
Oh.

191
00:06:45,530 --> 00:06:46,697
[pleasant music playing]

192
00:06:46,781 --> 00:06:48,699
Sir, I've already fixed the other room.

193
00:06:48,783 --> 00:06:51,327
Is that for Oka and me?

194
00:06:51,410 --> 00:06:52,537
Ah…

195
00:06:52,620 --> 00:06:54,747
Hey, we're together now.

196
00:06:54,831 --> 00:06:56,624
Psst, Jesabel, behave yourself.

197
00:06:56,707 --> 00:06:58,334
You're a lady.

198
00:06:58,417 --> 00:06:59,919
Sorry.

199
00:07:00,002 --> 00:07:01,462
No, it's just that you look like someone.

200
00:07:01,546 --> 00:07:02,839
Hmm? Who?

201
00:07:02,922 --> 00:07:04,924
Our future firstborn.

202
00:07:05,007 --> 00:07:06,384
[giggles]

203
00:07:06,467 --> 00:07:07,802
You won’t stop, huh.

204
00:07:07,885 --> 00:07:10,263
He's handsome, that's why.
[chuckles]

205
00:07:10,346 --> 00:07:11,097
Sorry.

206
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:12,348
Don't leave this place anymore, okay?

207
00:07:12,432 --> 00:07:14,392
Even after you've recovered, because…

208
00:07:14,475 --> 00:07:16,018
whenever Sir Atoy is busy,

209
00:07:16,102 --> 00:07:20,022
I'll ask you to teach me
how to be a great tracker instead.

210
00:07:20,106 --> 00:07:21,190
Tracker?

211
00:07:21,274 --> 00:07:22,775
What's that?

212
00:07:22,859 --> 00:07:24,527
[tense music playing]

213
00:07:24,610 --> 00:07:28,322
[suspicious music playing]

214
00:07:29,991 --> 00:07:31,492
Weren't you under…

215
00:07:31,576 --> 00:07:32,994
under Sir Mercado before?

216
00:07:33,077 --> 00:07:34,454
- OSCAR: Mmm-hmm.
- Didn't the two of you work together?

217
00:07:34,537 --> 00:07:36,664
You were a member of the army too, right?

218
00:07:36,747 --> 00:07:38,624
Oh, I thought maybe you served together--

219
00:07:38,708 --> 00:07:40,334
Ah, don't you have something to do?

220
00:07:40,418 --> 00:07:42,003
Buddy, the guys prepared some drinks.

221
00:07:42,086 --> 00:07:43,963
So you can finally meet them, since
you're going to be around for a while.

222
00:07:44,422 --> 00:07:46,591
- I thought you weren't going to treat us.
- Everything's ready actually.

223
00:07:46,674 --> 00:07:47,800
- All right. Come on, buddy.
- I'm coming. I don't have anything to do.

224
00:07:47,884 --> 00:07:49,385
ATOY: Huh? All right, all right.

225
00:07:49,469 --> 00:07:51,012
Oh. Sir Atoy!

226
00:07:51,095 --> 00:07:53,681
Let him try Kurt's braised beef.

227
00:07:53,764 --> 00:07:54,599
ATOY: Sure!

228
00:07:55,183 --> 00:07:55,892
Psst. That-- that-- that's enough.

229
00:07:55,975 --> 00:07:57,185
He's so handsome!

230
00:07:57,268 --> 00:08:00,813
Why did you bring up that
tracker training thing?

231
00:08:00,897 --> 00:08:02,398
He doesn't know anything about that.

232
00:08:02,482 --> 00:08:03,649
Oh, he doesn't?

233
00:08:04,692 --> 00:08:05,610
What’s the matter with you.

234
00:08:05,693 --> 00:08:07,195
Sorry.

235
00:08:07,278 --> 00:08:08,613
He's so handsome.

236
00:08:08,696 --> 00:08:10,072
Very!

237
00:08:10,156 --> 00:08:11,991
[suspicious music playing]

238
00:08:13,242 --> 00:08:15,661
We're definitely having a date at
Kurt's Pares place.

239
00:08:16,162 --> 00:08:17,663
ATOY: Ma'am, we're buying all of these.

240
00:08:17,747 --> 00:08:18,623
We’ll get everything.

241
00:08:18,706 --> 00:08:19,832
PALDO: There's Atoy.

242
00:08:19,916 --> 00:08:22,877
- Of course. Here’s the down payment.
- Atoy!

243
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:24,378
We're setting up a drinking session.

244
00:08:24,462 --> 00:08:25,087
Oh?

245
00:08:25,171 --> 00:08:26,464
There's karaoke too.

246
00:08:27,632 --> 00:08:29,175
Add this beer chow, okay?

247
00:08:29,258 --> 00:08:31,552
- We've bought everything.
- Oh, yeah.

248
00:08:31,636 --> 00:08:33,012
Any particular drink you want?

249
00:08:33,095 --> 00:08:35,139
I heard you haven't had a drink
in ten years.

250
00:08:35,223 --> 00:08:36,557
What do you want?

251
00:08:36,641 --> 00:08:38,059
Nah, it's not about the alcohol.

252
00:08:38,142 --> 00:08:39,435
It's about the company.

253
00:08:39,519 --> 00:08:40,394
Well…

254
00:08:40,478 --> 00:08:41,687
- Your friend is all right.
- Pretty good, huh?

255
00:08:41,771 --> 00:08:43,105
OSCAR: Of course. I just want to…

256
00:08:43,189 --> 00:08:44,106
get to know all of you,

257
00:08:44,190 --> 00:08:45,942
until we're all throwing up.

258
00:08:46,025 --> 00:08:47,318
PALDO: Nice.

259
00:08:47,401 --> 00:08:49,237
Buddy, the people here in Tabang Lupa,

260
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:51,864
the people in our barangay,
they're happy people.

261
00:08:51,948 --> 00:08:52,782
We've been through a lot together,

262
00:08:52,865 --> 00:08:55,034
so we're like one big family here.

263
00:08:55,117 --> 00:08:57,495
So don't worry,
and don't be shy around them, okay?

264
00:08:57,578 --> 00:08:58,246
They're all easygoing folks.

265
00:08:58,329 --> 00:08:59,163
[chuckles]

266
00:08:59,247 --> 00:09:00,414
So, okay? Join us.

267
00:09:00,498 --> 00:09:01,290
- OSCAR: Sure.
- We'll follow. We'll follow.

268
00:09:01,374 --> 00:09:02,708
- MUNGGO: Yeah.
- All right.

269
00:09:02,792 --> 00:09:03,793
PALDO: Let's go.

270
00:09:04,544 --> 00:09:06,295
[light music playing]

271
00:09:08,130 --> 00:09:09,465
- Ah, ah… Miss Cita, Miss.
- Oh. Mmm?

272
00:09:09,549 --> 00:09:11,884
Uhm, have you seen Atoy?

273
00:09:12,510 --> 00:09:14,220
Oh, he's still at the shop.

274
00:09:14,303 --> 00:09:16,764
Looks like he'll have drinks with Oscar,

275
00:09:16,847 --> 00:09:19,225
and Oscar will be staying there for now.

276
00:09:19,308 --> 00:09:22,853
My God! Atoy is so stubborn!

277
00:09:22,937 --> 00:09:25,273
I've already warned him about Oscar.

278
00:09:26,023 --> 00:09:27,650
But he just won't listen.

279
00:09:27,733 --> 00:09:29,652
Nothing. He ignores me.

280
00:09:30,403 --> 00:09:31,696
He seems nice, though.

281
00:09:31,779 --> 00:09:32,446
Oscar?

282
00:09:32,530 --> 00:09:35,992
Besides, he wouldn't be Atoy's friend
if he were a bad person.

283
00:09:36,075 --> 00:09:37,994
[pensive music playing]

284
00:09:38,077 --> 00:09:41,497
Audrey, I'm not trying to meddle.

285
00:09:41,581 --> 00:09:43,916
I've already mentioned this to Atoy.

286
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,294
You two just got married.

287
00:09:46,377 --> 00:09:47,044
Sooner or later,

288
00:09:47,128 --> 00:09:50,214
your differences in personality
will start to show.

289
00:09:50,298 --> 00:09:52,091
But as husband and wife,

290
00:09:52,174 --> 00:09:55,261
you need to know
how to listen to each other,

291
00:09:55,344 --> 00:09:56,971
understand each other,

292
00:09:57,054 --> 00:09:59,140
and learn to compromise.

293
00:09:59,223 --> 00:10:00,349
[music continues]

294
00:10:00,433 --> 00:10:02,310
Hmm?

295
00:10:03,477 --> 00:10:06,230
[music continues]

296
00:10:06,314 --> 00:10:07,565
Atoy, may I ask.

297
00:10:07,648 --> 00:10:08,899
What was that…

298
00:10:08,983 --> 00:10:10,192
thing Jesabel mentioned earlier?

299
00:10:10,276 --> 00:10:11,527
About…

300
00:10:11,611 --> 00:10:12,486
was it tracker?

301
00:10:12,570 --> 00:10:13,487
What is that?

302
00:10:14,113 --> 00:10:16,574
Is it connected to Colonel Mercado?

303
00:10:16,657 --> 00:10:17,700
Is he still active?

304
00:10:18,451 --> 00:10:21,203
Sir Mercado? Ah, no.
Not anymore.

305
00:10:22,371 --> 00:10:24,498
Actually, we don't even know where he is.

306
00:10:26,250 --> 00:10:29,337
I don't know if his disappearance
has anything to do with…

307
00:10:30,171 --> 00:10:32,006
Belladonna.

308
00:10:32,089 --> 00:10:33,007
Belladonna?

309
00:10:33,090 --> 00:10:36,052
Because that was the last thing…
we talked about.

310
00:10:37,094 --> 00:10:39,180
He told me to find Belladonna.

311
00:10:39,805 --> 00:10:40,640
[suspicious music playing]

312
00:10:40,723 --> 00:10:42,933
Do you know anything about Belladonna?

313
00:10:43,768 --> 00:10:45,936
Have you heard anything about it?

314
00:10:46,729 --> 00:10:48,022
Belladonna.

315
00:10:48,105 --> 00:10:50,066
[music continues]

316
00:10:50,149 --> 00:10:51,192
Doesn't ring a bell.

317
00:10:52,193 --> 00:10:53,611
OSCAR: No.
I never heard anything like that

318
00:10:53,694 --> 00:10:55,071
while I was with Obsidian.

319
00:10:55,571 --> 00:10:57,448
But you know, Toy,
it sounds like…

320
00:10:59,075 --> 00:11:00,576
something confidential.

321
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:02,620
Something classified, so…

322
00:11:02,703 --> 00:11:03,788
even though I was imprisoned there,

323
00:11:03,871 --> 00:11:06,290
they wouldn't have let me hear
about things like that.

324
00:11:06,374 --> 00:11:08,209
Those people never trusted me.

325
00:11:08,292 --> 00:11:09,752
Don't worry.

326
00:11:09,835 --> 00:11:11,379
We'll find it eventually.

327
00:11:11,462 --> 00:11:13,047
Ma'am, is it ready?

328
00:11:13,714 --> 00:11:15,299
ATOY: Make it extra crispy, okay?

329
00:11:15,383 --> 00:11:16,300
All right, just like before.

330
00:11:16,384 --> 00:11:17,426
That's it. Just like that.

331
00:11:17,510 --> 00:11:21,055
[thumping]

332
00:11:26,977 --> 00:11:29,021
I have bad news, Samir.

333
00:11:29,105 --> 00:11:31,816
[mysterious music playing]

334
00:11:32,358 --> 00:11:37,238
The local coast guard has sent divers
to inspect the sunken Grey Shadow.

335
00:11:38,781 --> 00:11:41,826
They have confiscated our gold and guns.

336
00:11:41,909 --> 00:11:44,036
[music continues]

337
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:45,246
And another thing.

338
00:11:45,329 --> 00:11:47,456
Guess who claimed Oscar at the hospital.

339
00:11:47,540 --> 00:11:49,166
[thumps]

340
00:11:49,250 --> 00:11:52,420
- Again and again, Anthony Padua.
- I know.

341
00:11:52,503 --> 00:11:54,713
[thumps]

342
00:11:54,797 --> 00:11:55,840
So, what's next?

343
00:11:55,923 --> 00:11:57,258
[thumps]

344
00:11:57,842 --> 00:11:59,969
[music continues]

345
00:12:00,052 --> 00:12:02,012
I think it's time

346
00:12:02,096 --> 00:12:04,223
to pay our prisoners a visit.

347
00:12:05,891 --> 00:12:09,645
We will make them tell us
who Belladonna is.

348
00:12:09,728 --> 00:12:12,314
[tense music playing]

349
00:12:18,487 --> 00:12:19,655
JANINE: Okay!

350
00:12:19,738 --> 00:12:20,865
It's ready.

351
00:12:21,574 --> 00:12:23,868
We have chicken tenders,

352
00:12:23,951 --> 00:12:25,536
and eggs and hotdogs.

353
00:12:25,619 --> 00:12:26,954
- What’s this?
- Your favorite.

354
00:12:27,037 --> 00:12:28,497
Hmm, dumplings.

355
00:12:29,123 --> 00:12:29,999
IBYANG: Dum-- dumplings?

356
00:12:30,082 --> 00:12:31,041
JANINE: And there's more.

357
00:12:31,125 --> 00:12:31,834
Pastries.

358
00:12:31,917 --> 00:12:33,502
That looks so good!

359
00:12:33,586 --> 00:12:35,254
[Janine chuckles softly]

360
00:12:35,337 --> 00:12:37,423
Mommy, are you okay?

361
00:12:38,757 --> 00:12:40,301
JANINE: What about Daddy?

362
00:12:40,384 --> 00:12:41,302
Has he come home yet?

363
00:12:42,344 --> 00:12:43,179
AUDREY: Uhm…

364
00:12:43,762 --> 00:12:45,723
Daddy Tatoy isn't home yet.

365
00:12:47,016 --> 00:12:48,434
He's still with Oscar.

366
00:12:49,393 --> 00:12:52,438
Isn't he staying here anymore?

367
00:12:54,899 --> 00:12:56,609
That's too bad.

368
00:12:56,692 --> 00:12:57,860
[soft drama music playing]

369
00:12:57,943 --> 00:13:00,404
He was actually fun to have around.

370
00:13:00,488 --> 00:13:02,740
And he's really nice, right?

371
00:13:04,158 --> 00:13:06,368
[music continues]

372
00:13:07,953 --> 00:13:09,413
Hmm, Mommy,

373
00:13:10,539 --> 00:13:14,001
why don't you want him to stay here?

374
00:13:14,835 --> 00:13:17,004
Our house is big enough.

375
00:13:17,087 --> 00:13:17,922
Exactly.

376
00:13:18,464 --> 00:13:19,924
And…

377
00:13:20,007 --> 00:13:24,261
Tatoy can spend time
with his best friend too.

378
00:13:25,721 --> 00:13:27,431
And Daddy said

379
00:13:27,932 --> 00:13:29,642
they're practically brothers.

380
00:13:30,893 --> 00:13:33,646
Hmm? They're kind of like us, Janine.

381
00:13:34,813 --> 00:13:36,649
Not related by blood, but…

382
00:13:36,732 --> 00:13:39,026
we treat each other like sisters.

383
00:13:40,444 --> 00:13:44,532
Janine Needle and Ibyang Thread.

384
00:13:44,615 --> 00:13:46,784
[music continues]

385
00:13:46,867 --> 00:13:49,787
I don't want to be separated
from my sister, Mama.

386
00:13:51,830 --> 00:13:56,335
That's why I'm sure Tatoy feels

387
00:13:56,418 --> 00:13:57,586
the same way about Uncle Oka.

388
00:13:57,670 --> 00:13:58,671
Correct.

389
00:14:00,339 --> 00:14:01,674
- JANINE: Let's eat?
- Yes.

390
00:14:01,757 --> 00:14:03,467
IBYANG: Oh, do you want to try some?

391
00:14:03,551 --> 00:14:04,426
JANINE: Croissant.

392
00:14:04,510 --> 00:14:06,136
[laughing & singing]

393
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:09,139
[lively chatter]

394
00:14:09,223 --> 00:14:11,809
ATOY: All right. Oh.

395
00:14:14,562 --> 00:14:16,480
What do you call…

396
00:14:17,356 --> 00:14:18,816
a soldier…

397
00:14:20,192 --> 00:14:21,402
who pays a visit?

398
00:14:22,111 --> 00:14:23,112
OTHERS: What?!

399
00:14:23,904 --> 00:14:24,530
Well…

400
00:14:24,613 --> 00:14:26,031
[chuckles]

401
00:14:26,115 --> 00:14:27,700
[in Filipino] A “sundalaw”!

402
00:14:27,783 --> 00:14:30,786
[laughing & singing]
[lively chatter]

403
00:14:30,870 --> 00:14:31,787
So that's what it is, huh?

404
00:14:31,871 --> 00:14:33,247
[in Filipino] “Sun-- sundalaw”!
[in Filipino] “Sundalaw?

405
00:14:33,330 --> 00:14:34,582
That sounds familiar!

406
00:14:34,665 --> 00:14:37,126
[laughing]
[lively chatter]

407
00:14:37,209 --> 00:14:39,044
Oh, I got one, I got one.

408
00:14:39,128 --> 00:14:39,712
I got one.

409
00:14:39,795 --> 00:14:40,421
- What is it?
- What? What is it? What is it?

410
00:14:40,504 --> 00:14:42,548
What do you call…

411
00:14:42,631 --> 00:14:44,216
a soldier who died?

412
00:14:44,300 --> 00:14:45,551
OTHERS: What?!

413
00:14:46,510 --> 00:14:47,887
A “soul-dier”!

414
00:14:47,970 --> 00:14:49,263
[laughs]

415
00:14:49,346 --> 00:14:50,055
Soul, soul--

416
00:14:50,139 --> 00:14:50,764
Soldier?

417
00:14:50,848 --> 00:14:52,057
- Yeah, soul…
- Soldier? Isn't that already a soldier?

418
00:14:52,141 --> 00:14:54,894
Spirit, soul, soul. Then “dier.”

419
00:14:54,977 --> 00:14:57,021
“Soul-dier.” “Soul-dier!”

420
00:14:57,104 --> 00:14:58,898
- [laughing]
- You guys okay over there?

421
00:14:58,981 --> 00:15:01,525
- Soul… “Soul-dier!”
- ATOY: You guys okay over there?

422
00:15:01,609 --> 00:15:03,485
- NESTOR: There you go!
- Ahh! I get it now!

423
00:15:03,569 --> 00:15:04,570
[laughing]
But that's a bit…

424
00:15:04,653 --> 00:15:05,362
3757.

425
00:15:05,446 --> 00:15:06,864
[lively chatter]
[laughing]

426
00:15:06,947 --> 00:15:08,490
Later, after you're done.

427
00:15:08,574 --> 00:15:09,742
[laughing]

428
00:15:09,825 --> 00:15:10,910
OSCAR: I'm okay with that.

429
00:15:10,993 --> 00:15:12,119
Uh, Oscar, wait.

430
00:15:12,202 --> 00:15:13,871
Let me change the subject.

431
00:15:13,954 --> 00:15:15,664
How were things…

432
00:15:15,748 --> 00:15:17,458
between you and Atoy back
when you were soldiers?

433
00:15:17,541 --> 00:15:18,876
Now that's a good one--

434
00:15:18,959 --> 00:15:20,586
PALDO: Now that's a great story!

435
00:15:20,669 --> 00:15:21,587
That's a great story!

436
00:15:22,796 --> 00:15:24,590
We were inseparable!

437
00:15:24,673 --> 00:15:25,257
[clears throat]

438
00:15:25,341 --> 00:15:26,467
Right, Toy--

439
00:15:27,343 --> 00:15:28,177
Wait, this.

440
00:15:29,094 --> 00:15:30,804
[singing nearby]

441
00:15:31,805 --> 00:15:34,099
He even gave me this…

442
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:37,269
Saint Anthony of Padua necklace.

443
00:15:37,353 --> 00:15:39,355
PALDO: Ooh! Nice!

444
00:15:39,939 --> 00:15:41,774
Yeah, he tied it around my neck himself.

445
00:15:41,857 --> 00:15:42,775
[chuckles]

446
00:15:43,859 --> 00:15:44,526
OSCAR: You know…

447
00:15:44,610 --> 00:15:46,070
this is true.

448
00:15:46,862 --> 00:15:49,907
With all the operations Atoy
and I went through together,

449
00:15:49,990 --> 00:15:51,408
I know him inside and out.

450
00:15:52,326 --> 00:15:53,535
His body language,

451
00:15:54,787 --> 00:15:56,413
how far he pees.

452
00:15:56,497 --> 00:15:57,539
- [laughs]
- OTHERS: Ah! Ahh!

453
00:15:57,623 --> 00:15:58,916
Shh!

454
00:15:58,999 --> 00:15:59,625
He's like a small skyrocket.

455
00:15:59,708 --> 00:16:01,001
NESTOR: A small skyrocket?
[chuckles]

456
00:16:01,085 --> 00:16:02,127
PALDO: More like a fountain.

457
00:16:02,670 --> 00:16:04,964
Even the number of times he snores.

458
00:16:06,882 --> 00:16:07,841
I know that too.

459
00:16:07,925 --> 00:16:09,677
PALDO: Ohh!

460
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:10,594
You know that?

461
00:16:11,095 --> 00:16:11,720
[laughs]

462
00:16:11,804 --> 00:16:15,224
Oka, out of all the missions

463
00:16:15,307 --> 00:16:16,767
you and Atoy went on,

464
00:16:16,850 --> 00:16:18,894
which one will you never forget?

465
00:16:18,978 --> 00:16:19,561
That's a good one.

466
00:16:19,645 --> 00:16:21,021
That's a great question.

467
00:16:21,105 --> 00:16:22,022
There were so many.

468
00:16:22,982 --> 00:16:24,817
Yeah, so many. There was, uhm…

469
00:16:25,693 --> 00:16:28,362
that time we captured rebels in Agusan.

470
00:16:28,445 --> 00:16:30,197
- PALDO: Oh?
- That one.

471
00:16:30,781 --> 00:16:32,116
OSCAR: And…

472
00:16:33,867 --> 00:16:36,078
those three siblings in Batangas.

473
00:16:36,161 --> 00:16:37,246
We rescued them.

474
00:16:37,329 --> 00:16:38,205
There were so many, Paldo.

475
00:16:38,288 --> 00:16:38,956
So many.

476
00:16:39,039 --> 00:16:41,750
- Really? That's awesome.
- It's hard to choose.

477
00:16:42,292 --> 00:16:43,752
[pensive music playing]

478
00:16:43,836 --> 00:16:45,546
But there is…

479
00:16:46,964 --> 00:16:49,925
one rescue mission, ten years ago.

480
00:16:50,009 --> 00:16:52,136
That's the one I'll never forget.

481
00:16:52,219 --> 00:16:53,971
[music continues]

482
00:16:55,639 --> 00:16:57,474
OSCAR: Because that's when I realized…

483
00:16:57,558 --> 00:16:59,685
that it's not about…

484
00:17:00,894 --> 00:17:02,354
how long you've known someone.

485
00:17:02,438 --> 00:17:06,442
That's not what determines
whether a person is truly your friend.

486
00:17:06,525 --> 00:17:09,194
[tense music playing]

487
00:17:09,862 --> 00:17:11,363
[music continues]

488
00:17:11,989 --> 00:17:14,116
Because this awesome friend of yours…

489
00:17:15,617 --> 00:17:16,910
he abandoned me.

490
00:17:18,787 --> 00:17:21,373
He left me there to die.

491
00:17:22,124 --> 00:17:23,459
Isn't that right, Atoy?

492
00:17:24,835 --> 00:17:27,254
[music swells]

493
00:17:35,512 --> 00:17:39,725
Because this awesome friend of yours…

494
00:17:40,642 --> 00:17:42,019
made me a promise.

495
00:17:43,520 --> 00:17:44,980
No one gets left behind.

496
00:17:45,731 --> 00:17:47,566
[pensive music playing]

497
00:17:47,649 --> 00:17:48,442
OSCAR: But what did you do?

498
00:17:48,525 --> 00:17:49,485
[sniffs]

499
00:17:49,568 --> 00:17:50,319
Hmm?

500
00:17:50,402 --> 00:17:51,987
[music continues]

501
00:17:53,655 --> 00:17:55,115
What did you do?

502
00:17:55,699 --> 00:17:57,701
[music continues]

503
00:17:58,368 --> 00:18:04,374
You left me in the middle of the battle
so you could save yourself.

504
00:18:04,458 --> 00:18:05,626
[music continues]

505
00:18:05,709 --> 00:18:07,294
You let me get bombed,

506
00:18:07,377 --> 00:18:09,379
even though you knew I was still alive.

507
00:18:10,881 --> 00:18:13,300
You left me there to die, didn't you?

508
00:18:14,885 --> 00:18:16,220
Atoy?

509
00:18:16,303 --> 00:18:17,262
[music continues]

510
00:18:18,347 --> 00:18:19,807
This guy's incredible.

511
00:18:20,390 --> 00:18:21,850
Let's all give him a round of applause.

512
00:18:21,934 --> 00:18:23,936
Amazing. Outstanding.
[applauds]

513
00:18:24,019 --> 00:18:24,728
[chuckles sarcastically]

514
00:18:24,812 --> 00:18:26,355
- PALDO: Okay, that's enough.
- That's not true, buddy.

515
00:18:26,438 --> 00:18:28,315
OSCAR: No, that's not--
[lively chatter]

516
00:18:28,398 --> 00:18:30,901
Let's do a shot! Shot, shot, shot!

517
00:18:30,984 --> 00:18:32,319
I'm still talking here. Wait, wait.

518
00:18:32,402 --> 00:18:33,529
Don't contradict me, buddy.

519
00:18:34,696 --> 00:18:36,031
They were asking me.

520
00:18:37,616 --> 00:18:38,242
Hmm?

521
00:18:38,325 --> 00:18:39,701
Buddy…

522
00:18:40,452 --> 00:18:41,203
OSCAR: Oh?

523
00:18:41,286 --> 00:18:43,205
We've already talked about this.

524
00:18:44,039 --> 00:18:45,290
I didn't leave you behind.

525
00:18:45,374 --> 00:18:46,834
[heavy music playing]

526
00:18:46,917 --> 00:18:50,087
I thought I was talking to you
on the radio.

527
00:18:50,170 --> 00:18:52,798
But you got fed fake news, didn't you?!

528
00:18:52,881 --> 00:18:54,591
[music continues]

529
00:18:54,675 --> 00:18:55,717
You got fooled, didn't you?!

530
00:18:55,801 --> 00:18:58,762
You believed them right away!

531
00:18:58,846 --> 00:19:03,684
How can you live with yourself every day
knowing you left me there to die?

532
00:19:03,767 --> 00:19:04,685
Hmm?

533
00:19:04,768 --> 00:19:05,727
[tense music playing]

534
00:19:05,811 --> 00:19:07,980
Because you've got a great life here.

535
00:19:08,063 --> 00:19:08,897
[music continues]

536
00:19:08,981 --> 00:19:11,191
Right? You have a business, a family,

537
00:19:11,275 --> 00:19:14,153
drinking buddies, friends.

538
00:19:14,236 --> 00:19:15,779
[music continues]

539
00:19:15,863 --> 00:19:18,824
While I spent ten years
suffering because of you!

540
00:19:18,907 --> 00:19:20,826
[music continues]

541
00:19:20,909 --> 00:19:23,203
Buddy, we've already talked about this.

542
00:19:23,287 --> 00:19:24,454
Then again, even now,

543
00:19:24,538 --> 00:19:26,707
you'd still leave me behind,
wouldn't you?

544
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:30,169
You couldn't even defend me against your…
[sniffs]

545
00:19:30,252 --> 00:19:32,212
accusive wife.

546
00:19:32,296 --> 00:19:33,338
That's not true, buddy.

547
00:19:33,422 --> 00:19:34,256
OSCAR: Hmm?

548
00:19:34,923 --> 00:19:36,258
Uhm, Oka?…

549
00:19:36,341 --> 00:19:37,968
looks like…

550
00:19:38,051 --> 00:19:38,969
What?

551
00:19:39,052 --> 00:19:40,762
Looks like you've had
a little too much to drink.

552
00:19:40,846 --> 00:19:42,097
Want us to take you inside?

553
00:19:42,181 --> 00:19:43,599
I'm not drunk.
Don't touch me.

554
00:19:43,682 --> 00:19:44,892
[heavy music playing]

555
00:19:44,975 --> 00:19:46,977
Paldo, Paldo. Buddy, buddy--

556
00:19:47,060 --> 00:19:47,644
Paldo.

557
00:19:47,728 --> 00:19:48,687
MUNGGO: Take him home, Toy!

558
00:19:48,770 --> 00:19:50,981
I've got this. I've got this.

559
00:19:52,399 --> 00:19:53,650
Come on. Let's head inside.

560
00:19:53,734 --> 00:19:55,527
SIONY: Go on, Paldo, bring him home!

561
00:19:55,611 --> 00:19:56,945
That's enough, Paldo.

562
00:19:57,029 --> 00:19:57,529
Sir Nestor.

563
00:19:57,613 --> 00:19:58,614
[indistinct chatter]

564
00:19:58,697 --> 00:19:59,740
Buddy, come on. Let's go inside--

565
00:19:59,823 --> 00:20:00,991
Don't touch me!

566
00:20:01,909 --> 00:20:03,243
- Come on, come on.
- I've got this!

567
00:20:03,327 --> 00:20:04,703
EMERSON: Take him home, Toy!

568
00:20:04,786 --> 00:20:06,163
NESTOR: Take him home, Toy!

569
00:20:06,747 --> 00:20:07,247
[indistinct chatter]

570
00:20:07,331 --> 00:20:08,248
- Come on, get inside--
- Don't touch me!

571
00:20:08,332 --> 00:20:08,832
SIONY: Oh!

572
00:20:08,916 --> 00:20:09,708
JONA: He's had too much.

573
00:20:09,791 --> 00:20:10,834
Buddy, come on. I'll take you--

574
00:20:10,918 --> 00:20:11,418
NESTOR: Oh!

575
00:20:11,501 --> 00:20:13,337
[thumps]
OTHERS: Hey! Oh, Toy!

576
00:20:14,004 --> 00:20:17,216
[panicking & screaming]

577
00:20:17,299 --> 00:20:19,301
Aargh!
NESTOR: Come on! Come on!

578
00:20:19,384 --> 00:20:21,345
[panicking]

579
00:20:21,428 --> 00:20:22,846
Buddy! Let's stop this!

580
00:20:23,555 --> 00:20:24,431
Stop your face!

581
00:20:24,514 --> 00:20:26,141
EMERSON: He's even worse when he's drunk!

582
00:20:26,225 --> 00:20:26,934
Stop them!

583
00:20:27,017 --> 00:20:27,935
SIONY: Break it up!

584
00:20:28,018 --> 00:20:28,685
[indistinct chatter]

585
00:20:28,769 --> 00:20:29,353
[growls]

586
00:20:29,436 --> 00:20:30,437
[gasps]

587
00:20:31,188 --> 00:20:32,481
[grunts]
[panicking]

588
00:20:35,234 --> 00:20:37,152
Come on, come on! What?

589
00:20:37,694 --> 00:20:39,154
[panicking]

590
00:20:39,238 --> 00:20:40,614
[music continues]

591
00:20:40,697 --> 00:20:41,406
Give him a lesson, Atoy!

592
00:20:41,490 --> 00:20:43,742
[growling & grunting]

593
00:20:43,825 --> 00:20:45,452
[thumping]

594
00:20:46,411 --> 00:20:47,496
Buddy, that's enough.

595
00:20:47,579 --> 00:20:49,248
[growls & grunts]

596
00:20:49,331 --> 00:20:50,916
[jeering]

597
00:20:50,999 --> 00:20:52,542
SIONY: Whoever loses…

598
00:20:52,626 --> 00:20:53,752
Whoever loses has to sing "Versace"!

599
00:20:53,835 --> 00:20:54,753
Has to sing "Versace"!

600
00:20:54,836 --> 00:20:55,921
That's a high song!

601
00:20:56,004 --> 00:20:57,130
Atoy, fight back!

602
00:20:57,214 --> 00:20:58,924
[growls & grunts]
[thuds]

603
00:20:59,007 --> 00:21:00,634
OTHER: Oh! Ohh!

604
00:21:00,717 --> 00:21:02,719
EMERSON: Looks like you're going down!
NESTOR: What now?!

605
00:21:02,803 --> 00:21:03,387
What?!

606
00:21:03,470 --> 00:21:04,721
- ATOY: That's enough.
- PALDO: That's enough.

607
00:21:04,805 --> 00:21:06,348
[coughs]

608
00:21:06,431 --> 00:21:07,224
EMERSON: You're so dramatic.

609
00:21:07,307 --> 00:21:08,642
NESTOR: There! Knockout!

610
00:21:08,725 --> 00:21:10,143
EMERSON: You're so dramatic.

611
00:21:10,227 --> 00:21:12,020
- JONA: That's what you get.
- I don't need your help!

612
00:21:12,104 --> 00:21:14,022
[pensive music playing]

613
00:21:14,106 --> 00:21:15,065
PALDO: Hey, psst.

614
00:21:15,148 --> 00:21:15,983
That's enough, all right?

615
00:21:16,066 --> 00:21:16,942
We're just having drinks here.

616
00:21:17,025 --> 00:21:18,610
We're supposed to be having fun!

617
00:21:19,736 --> 00:21:21,196
NESTOR: More drinks!
EMERSON: That's enough!

618
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:21,989
JONA: Don't be like that.

619
00:21:22,072 --> 00:21:22,990
Serves you right.

620
00:21:23,073 --> 00:21:24,324
- That's enough, okay?
- Pull him away, Captain!

621
00:21:24,408 --> 00:21:25,826
Let's just forget about it.

622
00:21:26,702 --> 00:21:29,121
[music continues]

623
00:21:29,871 --> 00:21:33,292
NESTOR: Time to go home!
[indistinct chattering]

624
00:21:33,375 --> 00:21:39,589
[indistinct chattering]
SIONY: That's enough, that's enough.

625
00:21:40,299 --> 00:21:41,591
[music continues]

626
00:21:46,013 --> 00:21:49,683
Love, can we make up now?

627
00:21:51,476 --> 00:21:53,812
I'm sorry for the things I said earlier.

628
00:21:55,605 --> 00:21:58,233
I want to apologize to Oscar too.

629
00:21:59,776 --> 00:22:02,946
Maybe I was wrong about him.

630
00:22:03,030 --> 00:22:04,740
[teacup clinks]

631
00:22:06,533 --> 00:22:08,869
- [utensils clatter]
- You won't be able to tell him that.

632
00:22:10,162 --> 00:22:10,996
[clears throat]

633
00:22:11,079 --> 00:22:12,414
He's gone. He already left.

634
00:22:13,582 --> 00:22:14,666
We even got into a fight.

635
00:22:14,750 --> 00:22:17,502
What? Why?

636
00:22:18,170 --> 00:22:20,422
He's still upset with me because

637
00:22:20,505 --> 00:22:22,716
I left him behind.

638
00:22:24,509 --> 00:22:26,219
I've regretted that ever since.

639
00:22:26,303 --> 00:22:28,305
[pensive music playing]

640
00:22:29,556 --> 00:22:32,100
You know, the situation back then
was just different.

641
00:22:33,018 --> 00:22:34,436
It was a very difficult situation,

642
00:22:34,519 --> 00:22:35,854
and that's why I did it.

643
00:22:35,937 --> 00:22:37,564
[soft drama music playing]

644
00:22:38,732 --> 00:22:40,734
That's why I wanted to make it up to him.

645
00:22:41,902 --> 00:22:42,778
[clicks tongue]

646
00:22:42,861 --> 00:22:43,862
But it doesn't matter now.

647
00:22:43,945 --> 00:22:45,572
He doesn't want anything to do with me.

648
00:22:46,490 --> 00:22:47,657
Now…

649
00:22:48,408 --> 00:22:50,243
I understand you.

650
00:22:51,661 --> 00:22:55,582
That's why you wanted him
to stay here so badly.

651
00:22:56,249 --> 00:22:58,502
Not just to make it up to him,

652
00:22:59,669 --> 00:23:00,504
but…

653
00:23:01,880 --> 00:23:02,798
for yourself too.

654
00:23:04,925 --> 00:23:07,177
So you could finally forgive yourself

655
00:23:07,260 --> 00:23:08,428
for leaving him behind.

656
00:23:08,512 --> 00:23:10,889
[melodramatic music playing]

657
00:23:10,972 --> 00:23:12,099
Maybe you're right.

658
00:23:13,642 --> 00:23:14,810
[clicks tongue] But it doesn't matter now.

659
00:23:14,893 --> 00:23:16,853
I don't know where to contact him

660
00:23:16,937 --> 00:23:18,396
or where to find him.

661
00:23:19,564 --> 00:23:21,483
[music continues]

662
00:23:22,818 --> 00:23:26,071
No matter what happens…

663
00:23:27,989 --> 00:23:30,242
I'll always consider him a friend.

664
00:23:35,205 --> 00:23:38,291
[music swells]

665
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:41,044
[dramatic music playing]

666
00:23:50,053 --> 00:23:55,976
[electronic blipping]
[intense music playing]

667
00:24:00,230 --> 00:24:01,606
Wait, wait. I'll talk.

668
00:24:01,690 --> 00:24:04,025
I was initially assigned to rescue

669
00:24:04,109 --> 00:24:05,193
Belladonna, but…

670
00:24:05,277 --> 00:24:05,902
But what?!

671
00:24:05,986 --> 00:24:08,697
It was given to someone else!

672
00:24:08,780 --> 00:24:09,447
[theme music playing]

673
00:24:09,531 --> 00:24:10,490
TRACKER: The Firefighter.

674
00:24:10,574 --> 00:24:12,284
Miss, don't scream!

675
00:24:12,367 --> 00:24:13,076
Help! Help!

676
00:24:13,160 --> 00:24:15,036
Psst, hey! Let her go.

677
00:24:15,120 --> 00:24:16,913
[grunting & groaning]
[thumping]

678
00:24:16,997 --> 00:24:19,666
Denden and I were going to visit Uno,

679
00:24:19,749 --> 00:24:22,210
but they said he's no longer in the ICU.

680
00:24:22,294 --> 00:24:23,795
Oh, all right.
Find out his room number.

681
00:24:23,879 --> 00:24:24,921
I'm heading there now.

682
00:24:25,005 --> 00:24:25,630
Don't leave, okay?

683
00:24:25,714 --> 00:24:27,132
I need to talk to Uno.

684
00:24:27,215 --> 00:24:27,924
What's going on?

685
00:24:28,008 --> 00:24:28,592
[bullet whizzes]
[groans]

686
00:24:28,675 --> 00:24:29,885
[thuds]

687
00:24:29,968 --> 00:24:31,386
["Mamang Sastre" playing]
